Chapter: ClassOpNoInstance
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 show and compare require an instance for their operand type. Box is a
 user type that derives nothing, so show and compare on it are each
 rejected with cdx-no-class-instance (CDX2052). Both helper bodies are
 checked even though only describe is called.

Section: Types

  Box =
    | Wrap (Integer) (Integer)

Section: Opening

  describe : Box -> Text
  describe (b) = show b

  ordering : Box, Box -> Integer
  ordering (a) (b) = compare a b

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (describe (Wrap 1 2))
  end

